==========================================================================
  V1 THE MEASUREMENT: the in-repo KMOS3D tail has 10 rows at z >= z* = 2.426; the V-channel contrast vs z < 2.30 is +0.009 dex (z = +0.30, footings pooled) -- the registered break (delta_zp(2 r_M) = -0.151 dex, closed form) is not resolved in-repo; the sigma0-channel contrast is +0.094 dex.
  V2 THE HONEST GEOMETRY: KMOS3D Vcirc sits at ~2.2 R_e INSIDE r_M on BOTH sides of z* (g_N ~ 3-10 a0 -- the Newtonian regime; galaxy_a0z for the same sample): the absolute level cannot carry the break; the registered falsifier (B07 iii) is a WITHIN-CATALOG discontinuity at z*, executable only with r > r_M points -- 10 in-repo rows are inside, and exactly ONE object (Big Wheel) is outside it.
  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT: the first execution of G08's registered 'z > z* dynamics test' on in-repo data.  The baryonic-floor prediction is a closed-form outer-radius statement -- delta_zp(r_ref) = 0.5 log10(r_M/r_ref), 0 at r_M, -0.1505 dex at 2 r_M -- and the in-repo sample CANNOT resolve it (radius-limited by design, P4); the z >= z* tail carries 8/10 heavy rotators, and the per-object freeze ladder (PART 2B) re-reads them as DRESSED: the massive tail froze early (own z* ~ 1.5-5+ per (1+z*) = 3.426 (sigma_ph/119.21)^2, G213), so the phantom is ALLOWED at their observed z and the high V/v_flat is its own share -- the 2.426 global break applies to MW-class masses this sample does not contain. Big Wheel (z = 3.25, the only in-repo r > r_M point above z*) carries f_dyn = 2.40 (DYN) / 1.30 (SED); under the per-object ladder its own freeze z* ~ 10.9 >> 3.25, so its phantom IS allowed -- CONSISTENT with the framework, no dust carrier required (the earlier 'dust-only' reading was the MW-class-registry mistake this lane corrects). K1, K2, K3 all recorded with their numbers; no kill fires on this channel; the ALMA CO outer-disk sample (N = 7-19 at 2 r_M, 3-5 sigma) is the named executable for the MW-class break.
